  "question": {
    "text": "An inductor coil and a capacitor and a resistance of 5 <math> <mrow> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi> </mrow> </math> are connected in series to an a.c. source of rms voltage 30 V. When the frequency of the source is varied, a maximum r.m.s. current of 5 A is observed. If this inductor is connected in parallel with a resistance 5 <math> <mrow> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi> </mrow> </math> to a battery of emf 25 V and internal resistance 2.0 <math> <mrow> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi> </mrow> </math>, the current drawn from the battery is",
